   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 3. Generate with a RefCap (Apply, cached)\n**H3 RefCap Apply (cached)** glues the RefCap's cached `<Picture i>` rows in front of a prompt that was encoded **without** the photos, and attaches the captured latents. The photos never go through the text encoder. The catch: natively the prompt's words attend to the photos, and here they can't. On the London Set faces that cost 0.01 of ArcFace similarity.\n\n**Use it when** you want to experiment with the two reference channels, or to keep the photo rows out of the text encoder. Otherwise prefer workflow 2 (Replay).\n\n**Wiring**\n- The prompt goes into *MiniMax H3 Reference to Video* with **no photos connected**; it also makes the latent.\n- The prompt must not contain other references. The node refuses conditioning that already has image rows.\n\n**Toggles** (for experiments)\n- `rows`: the text encoder's view of the photos.\n- `latents`: the compressed photos the video model attends to on every step. Latents alone kept more identity than rows alone.\n\n**Measured** (ArcFace face similarity to the photos; 2 London Set subjects x 2 scenes x 3 seeds, 608x352, 56 frames, on a community H3 turbo finetune at 8 steps):\n\n| path | vs native references (`match`) | recognisable as the person |\n|---|---|---|\n| native reference node | baseline (0.62-0.71) | 12/12 |\n| **H3 RefCap Replay** | identical, pixel for pixel | 12/12 |\n| Replay, RefCap captured from 1024 px photos with `max` | **+0.06**, higher in 12/12; ~2.2x render time, 163 MB file | 12/12 |\n| H3 RefCap Apply (cached) | -0.01 | 12/12 |\n| Apply, latents only / rows only | -0.08 / -0.27 | 12/12 |\n| RefMod Full Reference (ComfyUI-MiniMaxH3Mod, 1024 px) | +0.03 Apply, +0.05 Text Encode; the 1024 px RefCap beat its best path in 11/12 | 12/12 |\n| RefMod Compressed Reference | -0.60 to -0.62 | 0/12 |\n| no references | -0.66 | 0/12 |\n\n**More identity:** capture from ~1024 px photos with `ref_image_size` = `max`, if you can afford the render time. Details: `REFCAP_README.md` in ComfyUI-RefCap.\n\n**Settings in these workflows** follow ComfyUI's MiniMax H3 reference-to-video template: the ref2va model with its 4-step Lightning LoRA, 4 steps, `res_multistep` + `simple`, 608x352. For the base model, bypass the *Lightning LoRA* node and use 20 steps. The measurements quoted here ran on a community H3 turbo finetune (shift 6/3, 8 steps) on a 12 GB GPU. Raise the size and length for final renders; the reference tokens ride through every step, so more photos and larger captures cost time."
   ],
